# ROADMAP_NS_SEC — Static caps, SECRET sinks, path deny

File: openOODA/audit/roadmap_ns_sec.oot
Logline: Compares NORTHSTAR 4.2 and 4.5 plus SECURITY.oot to disk for fail-closed caps and SECRET process_exec.
Setup: Survey only. No product edit. No ROADMAP edit. C emit + gcc remains the product path.
Beats:
  1. Map each NORTHSTAR 4.2 cap class to SECURITY and to check, emit, and runtime.
  2. Map SECRET / IFC to check + emit-c + emit-llvm + emit-x86.
  3. Record path-jail and arg-flow proof.
  4. Recommend a 5.2 row only if a user binary misses deny for a wrong cap or a secret process_exec payload.

## 1. Production bar

  Production here means two user-binary facts:
    Missing or wrong cap fails closed on `oodac check` and on emit-c.
    A SECRET name must not reach `process_exec`.
  Full IFC lattice, SGX/TDX/SEV, and extra kernel object-cap beyond SHIPPED HMAC/seals
  are residual or already product. They are not a new open row.
  Do not add oodac leftover rows (5.3) or library leftover rows (5.4).
  Do not add moonshots.

## 2. Shared disk

  Check: `../ooda/oodac/check_caps.oo` + `check_cap_util.oo` + `check_cap_grant.oo`.
  Secret walk: `check_secret_println_sinks` in `c_emit_secret_check.oo`.
  Called from `check_drive.oo`, `c_emit.oo`, `llvm_emit.oo`, `x86_emit.oo`.
  Runtime seals: `../ooda/runtime/chs_rt_caps.c` (`oo_cap_require_*`, process-local tokens).
  Corpus: `../ooda/bootstrap/corpus/check/{pass,fail}/`.
  Hostile lock: `../ooda/scripts/hostile_cap_probe_smoke.oo`.
  SECURITY names `STATIC_CAPS.oot`. That file is not on disk. Seals live in `chs_rt_caps.c`.
  `SECRET_TAINT.oot` is not on disk. Sink names live in `c_emit_secret_alias.oo`.

## 3. NORTHSTAR 4.2 cap classes

  Format: clause | disk | production? | open?

  FsReadCap / FsWriteCap / FsCap
    NS 4.2 + SECURITY §2 / §4 (`read_file`, `write_file`, `path_exists`, `file_size`).
    Disk: fail `no_cap_read_file`, `no_cap_write_file`, `no_cap_path_exists`, `no_cap_file_size`,
    `wrong_granular_fsread_for_write`, `cap_arg_not_passed`. Pass `ok_fs_*`.
    Locks: `cap_g2_fs_granular_smoke.oo`, `caps_matrix_smoke.oo`.
    Runtime write jail: `chs_rt_fs.c` + `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` + `realpath`.
    Extra names in SECURITY (`fs_mkdir`, `fs_read_dir`, …) are runtime-sealed.
    They are not in `sealed_fs_kind_of`. Check does not treat them as free-call caps.
    Emit still forwards them. Runtime `oo_cap_require_fswrite` / `fsread` fail-closed.
    Production (named read/write/path/size): yes. Open: no.

  ProcessCap / SysCap
    NS 4.2 + SECURITY §1.1 / §4 (`sys_exec`, `process_exec`, spawn/wait/kill).
    Disk: fail `no_cap_sys_exec`, `no_cap_sys_spawn`, `wrong_granular_process_for_prctl`.
    Pass `ok_process_cap_sys_exec`, `ok_sys_cap_sys_exec`, `ok_sys_spawn`.
    `process_exec` maps to ProcessCap in `sealed_sys_kind_of`. Emit requires `&ProcessCap`
    and lowers to `oo_sys_exec` (`c_emit_sys.oo`). No corpus file named `no_cap_process_exec`.
    Same seal as `sys_exec`. Lock: `cap_g4_process_smoke.oo`.
    Production: yes. Open: no.

  EnvCap
    NS 4.2 + SECURITY `env_get`. Disk: `no_cap_env_get`, `ok_env_get`, `hostile_env_get.oo`.
    Runtime: `oo_process_policy_getenv` (OODA_/OO_ only). Hostile child drops `HOST_SECRET`.
    Production: yes. Open: no.

  NetCap / HttpCap / TcpCap / UdpCap / BindCap
    NS 4.2 + SECURITY §4. Disk: `no_cap_fetch`, `ok_http_cap_fetch`, `ok_net_cap_fetch_tcp`,
    `ok_tcp_cap_connect`, `wrong_granular_http_for_tcp`, `wrong_granular_tcp_for_fetch`.
    Lock: `cap_g1_net_granular_smoke.oo`. `sock_raw` is fail-closed residual (SECURITY).
    No corpus `no_cap_tcp_*`. Check still seals `tcp_connect` / bind / udp via `sealed_net_kind_of`.
    Production: yes. Open: no.

  TimeCap / RandCap / AllocCap
    NS 4.2 + SECURITY §4. Disk: `no_cap_now_ms`, `no_cap_sleep_ms`, `no_cap_random`,
    `no_cap_seed`, `no_cap_alloc_bytes` and matching pass files. Lock: `alloc_cap_smoke.oo`.
    Arena under AllocCap / `&ArenaCap` is SHIPPED product. Open: no.

  ThreadCap / GpuCap
    NS 4.2 + SECURITY §4. No files in `corpus/check/fail/` for these names.
    Disk: `libfloor_thread_gpu_smoke.oo`, `thread_join_smoke.oo`, `libfloor_mutex_thread_smoke.oo`.
    Bare `thread_spawn` / `gpu_launch` / `mutex_lock` refuse. Device GPU stays residual (5.1).
    Production (fail-closed missing cap): yes. Open: no.

  FfiCap / UnsafeFFICap
    NS 4.2 + SECURITY §2. Disk: `no_cap_dlopen`, `no_cap_chs_build`, `no_cap_host_ast_dump`,
    `ok_unsafe_ffi_dlopen`. Lock: `cap_ffi_product_floor_smoke.oo`. Production: yes. Open: no.

  Borrow / attenuate
    NS 4.2 borrow (`&Cap`) and attenuate. Disk: param `&Cap` + arg-flow (`cap_arg_wrong_name`).
    HMAC attenuate is SHIPPED product (`hostile_attenuate.oo`, OPEN-72). Kernel seals OPEN-73.
    SGX/TDX/SEV residual (SHIPPED §3, ROADMAP 5.1). Open: no.

## 4. NORTHSTAR 4.5 SECRET / IFC

  Clause: `SECRET:` tags; taint through assign, struct, and calls; block unsealed sinks
  (`process_exec`, unencrypted I/O, untrusted FFI).
  SECURITY §5: static taint is not a dynamic token. Distinct from caps.
  Disk (line-start `// SECRET: ident`, not type-level `#[Secret]`):
    `c_parse_secret_env`, `c_secret_is_sink_name` includes `process_exec`.
    Fail: `fixtures/secret_process_exec_fail.oo` plus alias, concat, struct-field, wrapper fails.
    Pass: `secret_process_exec_pass.oo`, `secret_struct_clean_process_exec_pass.oo`.
    SHIPPED: SECRET sinks include `process_exec`. Fail fixture refuses the secret.
    Lock: `scripts/secret_sink_enforce_smoke.oo` (emit-c `ERR\tsecret`).
    LLVM: `llvm_emit.oo` calls the same walk. `llvm_fail_closed_smoke.oo` refuses `secret_sink_fail`.
  Full IFC lattice and attribute IFC: residual in `c_emit_secret.oo`. Not a new production row.
  Production (`process_exec` deny on user check/emit-c): yes. Open: no.

## 5. Arg-flow and path traversal

  SECURITY §6 F01: first arg must be a declared cap ident.
  Disk: `cap_arg_not_passed.oo`, `cap_arg_wrong_name.oo`, `cap_name_not_type.oo`.
  Write path: `path_under_writedir` + `O_NOFOLLOW`. `..` basename denied.
  `ooda fix` / `ooda patch` refuse `..`, absolute paths, and symlinks (SHIPPED).
  `OODA_FS_READDIR` is named in SECURITY for reads. `oo_read_file` does not apply that jail.
  That is extra confinement, not a missing-cap hole. Not a 5.2 row.

## 6. Verdict

  Default-deny `E_CAP` / `ERR\tcapability` is on disk for the named 4.2 classes.
  A user binary that calls `process_exec` with a SECRET ident is refused on check and emit-c.
  HMAC attenuate and kernel seals are already SHIPPED. SGX and full IFC stay residual.
  C emit + gcc remains the product path.

## 7. Recommended open rows

  None.

  | id | title | why |
  |----|-------|-----|
  | —  | —     | Missing/wrong cap deny and SECRET→process_exec deny are on disk for a user binary. |
